  "findings": [
    "Original cluster Hindi and Unicode-record Hindi actually copy correctly in Chrome, although PDF.js inserts word-internal spaces for the original cluster file.",
    "Baseline simple RTL passes two extractor checks but actual Chrome full copy reverses word order.",
    "PDFKit full-run API is not a drop-in replacement for this corpus: Indic/Arabic mapping failures, RTL word order, and visible plus copied 123 becomes 321 in marked RTL.",
    "Whole-line ActualText yields exact full-copy text in all five fixtures and preserves pixels and drawing operators, but all six tested visible-word double-clicks select wrong text or nothing. This route is rejected for integration.",
    "Per-word ActualText and single-TJ/single-string variants retain RTL full-copy errors. Do not keep tuning these same representations without new evidence.",
    "Single-string mode omits inter-token corrections for diagnosis; pixel differences are recorded. It is not an approved typography change."
  ],
